$$ WinDbg script: log every D3DKMT kernel call the process makes, with its NTSTATUS, next to venera_d3d12's own
$$ debug output (OutputDebugString lines appear in the same log).
$$ Usage (admin PowerShell):
$$   WinDbgX.exe -c '$<Z:\win\kmt-trace.wds' Z:\win\panel\venera-panel.exe /run-test d3d12.copy
$$ (/run-test runs one of the panel's tests in the process itself; venera-panel /test lists them)
$$ then type g in WinDbg. When the process has exited: .logclose, and read C:\venera\kmt.log.
$$ A status other than 00000000 (or 00000103, STATUS_PENDING) is a failure.
$$ (WinDbgX stops a command file at the first "g", so the script only arms the breakpoints.)
.logopen C:\venera\kmt.log
.symfix
.reload
bm win32u!NtGdiDdDDI* ".printf \"%y\", @rip; gu; .printf \" -> %08x\\n\", @eax; g"
